(7268644, 1130644, 30364, '<td valign="top">I like this because it''s so witty (in part via the title), and because it''s such an original photograph, so perfectly composed and cropped to suit that whimsical reference.  I also like the l<i>ightness</i> of the rendering, where strength and assurance comes from apparent weakness and understatement: very Japanese!  So it''s the Order of the Thumb for you, and a thank you for the fascinating photograph.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a></td>', 'I like this because it''s so witty (in part via the title), and because it''s such an original photograph, so perfectly composed and cropped to suit that whimsical reference.  I also like the lightness of the rendering, where strength and assurance comes from apparent weakness and understatement: very Japanese!  So it''s the Order of the Thumb for you, and a thank you for the fascinating photograph.', '2014-10-02 16:37:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(7268651, 1131111, 30364, '<td valign="top">My favourite photograph in the challenge.  I think it''s a photograph that can only be taken with a cell phone camera.  I know that''s not literally true; any clever manipulator could make a ''real'' photograph look nearly this good in post, but this one just has the honesty of the real thing.  It''s a question of attitude, and your photograph has it.  Plus it''s a terrific composition and a very good, simple idea about the incidental relationship of one thing with another.  Nice dog, too.  Please give him (her?) this Order of the Thumb, and a biscuit.  Thank you.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a></td>', 'My favourite photograph in the challenge.  I think it''s a photograph that can only be taken with a cell phone camera.  I know that''s not literally true; any clever manipulator could make a ''real'' photograph look nearly this good in post, but this one just has the honesty of the real thing.  It''s a question of attitude, and your photograph has it.  Plus it''s a terrific composition and a very good, simple idea about the incidental relationship of one thing with another.  Nice dog, too.  Please give him (her?) this Order of the Thumb, and a biscuit.  Thank you.', '2014-10-02 16:45:17.000000', NULL, 1),
(7268763, 1130546, 50695, '<td valign="top">when I look at this picture, Organic Geometry is not one of the first things that comes to mind, thank goodness.<br/> <br/>What are the words that come to your mind? Be honest. <br/> <br/>It''s only fair I take my own challenge. Let''s see...<br/> <br/>Flying Nun caught in a spoon<br/> <br/>mother being cold to her son, who sits facing away from her as his face disappears<br/> <br/>cat robots taking over the world and making it fly<br/> <br/>Modernist bats mocking Surrealism<br/> <br/>armpit stain that looks like Jesus<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1077279" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg"/></a></td>', 'when I look at this picture, Organic Geometry is not one of the first things that comes to mind, thank goodness. What are the words that come to your mind? Be honest.  It''s only fair I take my own challenge. Let''s see... Flying Nun caught in a spoon mother being cold to her son, who sits facing away from her as his face disappears cat robots taking over the world and making it fly Modernist bats mocking Surrealism armpit stain that looks like Jesus ', '2014-10-02 22:54:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(7268764, 1130502, 50695, '<td valign="top">The organic sea cut up into geometry.<br/> <br/>The organic woman surrounded by geometry, staring into geometry.<br/> <br/>Woman at the window, like the one Dali painted.<br/> <br/>This photo has that empty quality, that waiting quality ...<br/> <br/>I''m hanging it in my fantasy art gallery<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1077279" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/50000-54999/50695/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1077279.jpg"/></a></td>', 'The organic sea cut up into geometry. The organic woman surrounded by geometry, staring into geometry. Woman at the window, like the one Dali painted. This photo has that empty quality, that waiting quality ... I''m hanging it in my fantasy art gallery ', '2014-10-02 22:58:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(7268834, 1130336, 30364, '<td valign="top">A wonderful photograph.  As in <i>wonder-filled.</i> There are so many interesting qualities - and so many deft decisions made  for us to admire.  <br/> <br/>Perspective is one; either you''re very short, or you were smart enough to make yourself momentarily shorter to obtain the perfect (though slightly unnatural but the viewer doesn''t realise that) eye line through the scene.  It''s something that cinematographers do by instinct, but not so many still photographers do it, except for the great ones.  <br/> <br/>The decision (probably close to inevitable I admit, but worth comment anyway) to have part-vehicles both entering and exiting the frame on the two sides has bracketed the two girls in the most dynamic yet subtle way.  Had you waited, as a lesser eye might have done, for the sides to be ''distraction-free'', some of the intimacy of your photograph would be leaking away out of the sides.<br/> <br/>The fact that the two girls are looking together away from you, rather than facing you, also makes the photograph more interesting; more voyeuristic. That''s key to the charm of this picture; that it is a non-intrusive peek into a relationship.  It''s a non-confrontational street photographic, and all the better for that lightness of breath.<br/> <br/>The processing for a nostalgic, old-film effect is very often inappropriately deployed, but not here ... it''s just perfect for gently elevating the emotional essence of this picture.<br/> <br/>And then there''s all the things that played right into your hands without your intervention or decision: the timeless style of the modest dresses, the sensible walking shoes, and the holding hands.<br/> <br/>It''s a lovely, memorable, enviable photograph.  Please accept an Order of the Thumb, a 10, and a thank you for the picture.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a></td>', 'A wonderful photograph.  As in wonder-filled. There are so many interesting qualities - and so many deft decisions made  for us to admire.   Perspective is one; either you''re very short, or you were smart enough to make yourself momentarily shorter to obtain the perfect (though slightly unnatural but the viewer doesn''t realise that) eye line through the scene.  It''s something that cinematographers do by instinct, but not so many still photographers do it, except for the great ones.   The decision (probably close to inevitable I admit, but worth comment anyway) to have part-vehicles both entering and exiting the frame on the two sides has bracketed the two girls in the most dynamic yet subtle way.  Had you waited, as a lesser eye might have done, for the sides to be ''distraction-free'', some of the intimacy of your photograph would be leaking away out of the sides. The fact that the two girls are looking together away from you, rather than facing you, also makes the photograph more interesting; more voyeuristic. That''s key to the charm of this picture; that it is a non-intrusive peek into a relationship.  It''s a non-confrontational street photographic, and all the better for that lightness of breath. The processing for a nostalgic, old-film effect is very often inappropriately deployed, but not here ... it''s just perfect for gently elevating the emotional essence of this picture. And then there''s all the things that played right into your hands without your intervention or decision: the timeless style of the modest dresses, the sensible walking shoes, and the holding hands. It''s a lovely, memorable, enviable photograph.  Please accept an Order of the Thumb, a 10, and a thank you for the picture.', '2014-10-03 03:31:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(7268863, 1131154, 30364, '<td valign="top">This is an uncommonly good and uncommonly interesting photograph for DPC. <br/> <br/>By that I mean that nearly everyone here is an admirer of unequivocal photography, and wants to produce nothing more  and certainly nothing less  than that themselves: The kind of stuff that really impresses the family and friends.  <br/> <br/>But not so many are brave enough, nor curious enough, to produce the slightly discordant stuff that sows doubt and confusion, including in themselves. Photographs like this fabulously insurrectionist picture, that resists immediate resolution and ferments restlessness of the imagination.<br/> <br/>It''s a world-class photograph.  Your score is therefore 10.95 and your burden is this Order of the Thumb.  Thank you.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a></td>', 'This is an uncommonly good and uncommonly interesting photograph for DPC.  By that I mean that nearly everyone here is an admirer of unequivocal photography, and wants to produce nothing more  and certainly nothing less  than that themselves: The kind of stuff that really impresses the family and friends.   But not so many are brave enough, nor curious enough, to produce the slightly discordant stuff that sows doubt and confusion, including in themselves. Photographs like this fabulously insurrectionist picture, that resists immediate resolution and ferments restlessness of the imagination. It''s a world-class photograph.  Your score is therefore 10.95 and your burden is this Order of the Thumb.  Thank you.', '2014-10-03 07:32:56.000000', NULL, 1),
