(7524491, 1202577, 30364, '<td valign="top">This is my favourite of the challenge, and by a handy stretch too.  Against the depicted and merely cited patriotic iconography  the stuff of brassy celebrations, of tub-thumping and facile expression  you have juxtaposed a plainly-lovely, contemplative girl (could be a young boy I suppose; doesn''t matter). And you''ve done it in monochrome too!  Such wonderful contradictions, such absorbing counterpoint.  A work of love and circumspection together. Patriotism for grown-ups, which is just what America needs at the moment. 10. Thank you.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a></td>', 'This is my favourite of the challenge, and by a handy stretch too.  Against the depicted and merely cited patriotic iconography  the stuff of brassy celebrations, of tub-thumping and facile expression  you have juxtaposed a plainly-lovely, contemplative girl (could be a young boy I suppose; doesn''t matter). And you''ve done it in monochrome too!  Such wonderful contradictions, such absorbing counterpoint.  A work of love and circumspection together. Patriotism for grown-ups, which is just what America needs at the moment. 10. Thank you.', '2017-07-20 14:39:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(7524512, 1202520, 61396, '<td valign="top">this is completely different. I like how the presentation supports the schizophrenic story. Now, as much as I fear of turning the page back to bloody chapter 7, I am even more worried about what chapter 9 will turn out to be.<br/> <br/>may this balloon give you some peace of mind<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=1154420" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/61396/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1154420.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/61396/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1154420.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/60000-64999/61396/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_1154420.jpg"/></a></td>', 'this is completely different. I like how the presentation supports the schizophrenic story. Now, as much as I fear of turning the page back to bloody chapter 7, I am even more worried about what chapter 9 will turn out to be. may this balloon give you some peace of mind', '2017-07-20 18:59:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(7524699, 1202678, 30364, '<td valign="top">Yes, I see you. This is very nearly the only entry where I can find even a mildly ambitious attempt at the figurative; at expressing what loneliness represents, how it feels and tastes.  At saying just how big some small things are.<br/> <br/>I''m normally an uncomplaining and extravagantly tolerant bloke (I''m noted for it, surely?), but it''s so depressing to see entry after entry in which aloneness is depicted as if it were synonymous with loneliness.  It''s OK to be imaginatively bankrupt, but please keep it to yourselves!<br/> <br/>I don''t mean you of course; you still have a few bucks in your imagination &amp; whimsy account, as evidenced here.  I was just hijacking your entry in order to have a bit of a rant.  Thank you for hosting my tantrum.  <br/> <br/>And as for your entry, it''s welcome and interesting, and it stimulates some reflection on the part of the viewer.  So ... it''s 10 for you. Thank you.<br/> <br/>P.S. Did you find this?  I slipped it under your door.<br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=800078" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/30000-34999/30364/120/Copyrighted_Image_Reuse_Prohibited_800078.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Yes, I see you. This is very nearly the only entry where I can find even a mildly ambitious attempt at the figurative; at expressing what loneliness represents, how it feels and tastes.  At saying just how big some small things are. I''m normally an uncomplaining and extravagantly tolerant bloke (I''m noted for it, surely?), but it''s so depressing to see entry after entry in which aloneness is depicted as if it were synonymous with loneliness.  It''s OK to be imaginatively bankrupt, but please keep it to yourselves! I don''t mean you of course; you still have a few bucks in your imagination & whimsy account, as evidenced here.  I was just hijacking your entry in order to have a bit of a rant.  Thank you for hosting my tantrum.   And as for your entry, it''s welcome and interesting, and it stimulates some reflection on the part of the viewer.  So ... it''s 10 for you. Thank you. P.S. Did you find this?  I slipped it under your door.', '2017-07-21 12:57:14.000000', NULL, 1),
